MICROSOFT AZURE DATA PROCESSING ADDENDUM
Microsoft Corporation

Effective Date: August 5, 2026
Customer: VisaCanada Inc.
Services: Azure Document Intelligence (Form Recognizer)

This Data Processing Addendum ("DPA") supplements the Microsoft Online Services Terms and governs Microsoft's processing of Customer Data.

1. DEFINITIONS
   "Customer Data" means all data provided to Microsoft through use of Azure Services.
   "Personal Data" means any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person.

2. DATA PROCESSING TERMS
   2.1 Microsoft will process Customer Data only to provide the Services and comply with Customer's documented instructions.
   2.2 Microsoft will not use Customer Data for advertising or similar commercial purposes.

3. DATA SECURITY
   3.1 Encryption:
       - At rest: AES-256 encryption for all stored data
       - In transit: TLS 1.2 or higher for all communications

   3.2 Access Controls:
       - Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
       - Multi-factor authentication for administrative access
       - Regular access reviews and audits

   3.3 Compliance Certifications:
       - ISO/IEC 27001, 27017, 27018
       - SOC 1, SOC 2, SOC 3
       - PIPEDA-compliant operations in Canada

4. DATA RESIDENCY
   4.1 Region: Canada Central (Toronto, Ontario)
   4.2 Customer Data will be stored and processed exclusively in the Canada Central region.
   4.3 Data Residency Lock: Configured to prevent data transfer outside Canada without explicit authorization.
   4.4 No cross-border transfers without Customer consent.

5. SUBPROCESSORS
   5.1 Microsoft may engage subprocessors listed at: https://aka.ms/online-services-terms
   5.2 Customer will be notified 30 days before any new subprocessor engagement.

6. DATA SUBJECT RIGHTS
   Microsoft will assist Customer in responding to data subject requests (access, correction, deletion, portability) within 30 days.

7. SECURITY BREACH NOTIFICATION
   7.1 Microsoft will notify Customer without undue delay and within 72 hours of becoming aware of a personal data breach affecting Customer Data.
   7.2 Notification will include:
       - Nature of the breach
       - Affected data categories
       - Likely consequences
       - Mitigation measures taken

8. AUDIT AND COMPLIANCE
   8.1 Azure Monitor logs available for Customer audit
   8.2 Annual SOC 2 Type II reports available via Service Trust Portal
   8.3 Customer may conduct on-site audits with 30 days notice (max once per year)

9. DATA DELETION
   9.1 Upon termination, Microsoft will delete all Customer Data within 90 days.
   9.2 Customer may request immediate deletion via Azure Portal.
   9.3 Backup copies deleted within 180 days per retention policy.

10. LIABILITY
    Each party's liability is limited as specified in the Microsoft Online Services Terms.

11. TERM
    This DPA is effective from August 5, 2026 to August 5, 2027 and renews automatically unless terminated.

AGREED AND ACCEPTED:

